<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa's Stals doesn't see big c.bank gold sales.</title>
<headline>S.Africa's Stals doesn't see big c.bank gold sales.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold sales by the central banks of Belgium and the Netherlands were unlikely to be duplicated by other central banks, South African Reserve Bank Governor Chris Stals said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think substantial sales like those are something of the past. I don't think we'll see much of it in future,&quot; he told a roadshow of local institutions in Cape Town.</p>
<p>Stals said he believed Belgium and the Netherlands were the only two countries which felt uncomfortable with the size of their gold portfolios.</p>
<p>Fears of central bank gold disposals have spooked the bullion market this year, sending the metal to its lowest level in 3-3/4 years.</p>
</text>
